cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "flooded" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'flooded: Map Floodplains from an Elevation Model and a Stream Network'
version: 0.8.1
abstract: Maps floodplains and unconfined valley bottoms from a digital elevation
  model and a stream network with the Valley Confinement Algorithm (VCA), keeping
  ground that is gentle, near a stream in both straight-line and slope-weighted distance,
  and low relative to it. It classifies terrain and does not simulate floods, so its
  output is a screening map, not a field-validated floodplain. Fetches an elevation
  model for an area, maps preset flood levels, and attributes one floodplain to each
  watercourse that shares it, carrying per-reach flags onto the ground beside each
  reach. Ported from the bcfishpass lateral habitat pipeline (Python) with origins
  in the USDA VCA Toolbox and BlueGeo. Under active development.
